WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.633 --> 00:00:05.834
There are other human
beings on Mars now.

00:00:05.834 --> 00:00:11.233
Coexistence may prove
just as challenging

00:00:11.233 --> 00:00:12.233
as it does on Earth.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.033
ELON MUSK: Mars
civilization ultimately

00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:20.734
looks like an advanced
version of Earth.

00:00:20.734 --> 00:00:22.700
SUSAN WISE BAUER: Industry
is going to be absolutely

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.633
vital to that effort.

00:00:25.633 --> 00:00:27.367
Lokrum is a
private corporation.

00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:30.633
And Linus, you're
here to make a profit.

00:00:30.633 --> 00:00:32.133
ANDY WEIR: If there's
money to be made,

00:00:32.133 --> 00:00:33.934
then people would go
there to make the money.

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:36.033
ANTONIA JUHASZ: The Arctic
is a perfect example of this.

00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:42.100
We see companies looking at the
Arctic as a porthole for oil.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.800
Space is the new frontier.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:47.633
It's unexploited.

00:00:47.633 --> 00:00:48.367
What's that saying?

00:00:48.367 --> 00:00:51.233
Drill, baby, drill?

00:00:51.233 --> 00:00:54.467
Your crew has cut into
a scientific preserve.

00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:56.667
What you're doing is not right.

00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:59.967
CASEY DREIER: Any time
science reaches a conclusion,

00:00:59.967 --> 00:01:02.567
you are going to face pushback.

00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:04.467
NEIL DEGRASSE TYSON: The
history of human conduct,

00:01:04.467 --> 00:01:08.200
we have plenty of evidence
of things going wrong.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:11.467
Who's side are you on?

00:01:11.467 --> 00:01:14.967
There are no real
boundaries here.

00:01:14.967 --> 00:01:16.934
Mars is going to
be more dangerous.

00:01:16.934 --> 00:01:19.066
There's a contagion going
through Lokrum colony.

00:01:19.066 --> 00:01:20.633
What the hell's
going on in there?

00:01:20.633 --> 00:01:24.000
ADAM FRANK: Consequences are
going to be dire for everybody.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.767
I don't know what to do.

00:01:25.767 --> 00:01:28.400
STEPHEN PETRANEK: The
cost of being foolish

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.500
is so high that you will fail.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:34.233
There's one thing
Mars teaches you.

00:01:34.233 --> 00:01:37.300
It's patience.

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:41.033
BILL NYE: Space exploration
brings out the best in us.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.300
It's where we
solve problems that

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:45.233
have never been solved before.

00:01:45.233 --> 00:01:47.633
No one can control
what happens on Mars.

00:01:50.767 --> 00:01:54.834
The planet has a way of making
sure actions have consequences.

